      "widgets_values": [
        "Photorealistic close-up of a mechanical water-meter digit register. Use <ref_image_0> exclusively as the spatial layout guide: preserve its overall canvas, exact digit-slot count, column ordering, spacing, and the positions and shapes of the individual digit windows. The black and white regions in the guide indicate layout only; do NOT render the black/white guide into the final image. Use <ref_image_1> through <ref_image_9> exclusively as appearance references for materials, printed digits, mechanical wheel texture, lighting, and camera realism. Render a realistic continuous multi-wheel numeral display, not annotation dots or colored outlines. Five digit windows, left to right: (1) 0 centered; (2) 4 centered; (3) a rolling transition 9 to 0, with 9 above and 0 below, about 20% progressed; (4) 6 centered; (5) a rolling transition 6 to 7, with 6 above and 7 below, about 70% progressed. Rolling progress t=0 means the current digit centered and t=1 means the next digit centered; the next digit follows modulo-10 order, including 9 to 0. Numbers must remain legible and physically plausible, including partially visible neighbors during transitions. Preserve each full vertical wheel strip and digit order. Generate only the photorealistic register image, with no text overlays, green markers, labels, bounding box outlines, or collage. The desired image degradation is applied downstream after VAE decoding, not inside the generative prompt."
